   "end": 39.76,
   "speaker": "speaker:0",
   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "Beyond the flexure, the jejunum makes up the proximal two-fifths, and the ileum, the distal three-fifths. There is no sharp border, but the character changes. The jejunum lies mostly in the left upper abdomen. Its wall is thicker, its lumen wider and redder, and its mucosa is packed with tall circular folds, which give a feathery pattern on barium. The ileum lies in the right lower abdomen and pelvis, with a thinner wall and fewer, lower folds. The mesentery tells them apart too. The jejunum has long vasa recta and only one or two arcades. The ileum has short vasa recta, many arcades, and more fat. And lymphoid Peyer's patches gather in the ileum."
  }
 ],
 "text": "Beyond the flexure, the jejunum makes up the proximal two-fifths, and the ileum, the distal three-fifths. There is no sharp border, but the character changes. The jejunum lies mostly in the left upper abdomen. Its wall is thicker, its lumen wider and redder, and its mucosa is packed with tall circular folds, which give a feathery pattern on barium. The ileum lies in the right lower abdomen and pelvis, with a thinner wall and fewer, lower folds. The mesentery tells them apart too. The jejunum has long vasa recta and only one or two arcades. The ileum has short vasa recta, many arcades, and more fat. And lymphoid Peyer's patches gather in the ileum."
